# Central dictation lexicon.
#
# Vocabulary that dictation gets wrong and that is not specific to one repository: names of
# people, tools and services that appear across projects. Per-project terms live in that
# repository's `.lexicon`; the two lists are merged at request time with the repo's terms first.
#
# Rules:
#   - One term per line. `#` starts a comment.
#   - Add a term only after it has been shown to fail without the list and to be fixed with it.
#     An unnecessary term consumes a slot at the provider's 100-term cap and dilutes the boost
#     the others receive.
#   - Plain English words do not belong here: they either already transcribe correctly or, like
#     `main`, cannot be boosted at all.
#   - Case is preserved in the output, so write the term the way it should read: `LiteLLM`, not
#     `litellm`.
#
# Consumed by the transcription shim, which reads the installed copy at ~/.paseo/lexicon.central.

Ashby
Paseo
Python
Makefile
PR
venv
LiteLLM
Vaultwarden
Tailscale
Deepgram
podman
restic
opencode
omp
pyrefly
omp-config
